{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol | sed -n '205,260p'; nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase.sol | sed -n '94,114p'\"","aggregated_output":"   205\t     *\n   206\t     * @param token The token targeted by the call.\n   207\t     * @param from The sender of the tokens\n   208\t     * @param to The recipient of the tokens\n   209\t     * @param value The amount of token to transfer\n   210\t     * @param bubble Behavior switch if the transfer call reverts: bubble the revert reason or return a false boolean.\n   211\t     */\n   212\t    function _safeTransferFrom(\n   213\t        IERC20 token,\n   214\t        address from,\n   215\t        address to,\n   216\t        uint256 value,\n   217\t        bool bubble\n   218\t    ) private returns (bool success) {\n   219\t        bytes4 selector = IERC20.transferFrom.selector;\n   220\t\n   221\t        assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n   222\t            let fmp := mload(0x40)\n   223\t            mstore(0x00, selector)\n   224\t            mstore(0x04, and(from, shr(96, not(0))))\n   225\t            mstore(0x24, and(to, shr(96, not(0))))\n   226\t            mstore(0x44, value)\n   227\t            success := call(gas(), token, 0, 0x00, 0x64, 0x00, 0x20)\n   228\t            // if call success and return is true, all is good.\n   229\t            // otherwise (not success or return is not true), we need to perform further checks\n   230\t            if iszero(and(success, eq(mload(0x00), 1))) {\n   231\t                // if the call was a failure and bubble is enabled, bubble the error\n   232\t                if and(iszero(success), bubble) {\n   233\t                    returndatacopy(fmp, 0x00, returndatasize())\n   234\t                    revert(fmp, returndatasize())\n   235\t                }\n   236\t                // if the return value is not true, then the call is only successful if:\n   237\t                // - the token address has code\n   238\t                // - the returndata is empty\n   239\t                success := and(success, and(iszero(returndatasize()), gt(extcodesize(token), 0)))\n   240\t            }\n   241\t            mstore(0x40, fmp)\n   242\t            mstore(0x60, 0)\n   243\t        }\n   244\t    }\n   245\t\n   246\t    /**\n   247\t     * @dev Imitates a Solidity `token.approve(spender, value)` call, relaxing the requirement on the return value:\n   248\t     * the return value is optional (but if data is returned, it must not be false).\n   249\t     *\n   250\t     * @param token The token targeted by the call.\n   251\t     * @param spender The spender of the tokens\n   252\t     * @param value The amount of token to transfer\n   253\t     * @param bubble Behavior switch if the transfer call reverts: bubble the revert reason or return a false boolean.\n   254\t     */\n   255\t    function _safeApprove(IERC20 token, address spender, uint256 value, bool bubble) private returns (bool success) {\n   256\t        bytes4 selector = IERC20.approve.selector;\n   257\t\n   258\t        assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n   259\t            let fmp := mload(0x40)\n   260\t            mstore(0x00, selector)\n    94\t   *\n    95\t   * @param _requestId is the VRF V2 request ID.\n    96\t   * @param _randomWords is the randomness result.\n    97\t   */\n    98\t  // solhint-disable-next-line chainlink-solidity/prefix-internal-functions-with-underscore\n    99\t  function fulfillRandomWords(uint256 _requestId, uint256[] memory _randomWords) internal virtual;\n   100\t\n   101\t  function rawFulfillRandomWords(uint256 _requestId, uint256[] memory _randomWords) external {\n   102\t    address vrfWrapperAddr = address(i_vrfV2PlusWrapper);\n   103\t    if (msg.sender != vrfWrapperAddr) {\n   104\t      revert OnlyVRFWrapperCanFulfill(msg.sender, vrfWrapperAddr);\n   105\t    }\n   106\t    fulfillRandomWords(_requestId, _randomWords);\n   107\t  }\n   108\t\n   109\t  /// @notice getBalance returns the native balance of the consumer contract\n   110\t  function getBalance() public view returns (uint256) {\n   111\t    return address(this).balance;\n   112\t  }\n   113\t\n   114\t  /// @notice getLinkToken returns the link token contract\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"A callback can activate the clone and buy entries before creation returns, provided the purchase and final escrow checks pass. A contract sponsor can also cancel an empty raffle during that window, but this changes its status and forces the factory call to roll back. No draw or VRF continuation starts from creation.\n"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"_kritt_extractor_helper\": true,\n  \"stub\": false,\n  \"stub_explanation\": \"\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Valid creation deploys and initializes a fixed-implementation clone, registers it, escrows the selected NFT, verifies activation and reported ownership, and returns the raffle address. Creation does not initiate a randomness request.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - ABI-decodes CreateRaffleParams and enters the factory's nonReentrant guard.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:154 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - checks deployed prize code, recipient and protocol destinations, ERC-721 interface support, and nonzero reserve.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:99 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - requires a future endTime no more than 30 days away.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:105 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - increments raffleCount and selects the immutable raffleImplementation for cloning.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol:57 Clones.clone - deploys an ERC-1167 proxy using CREATE with zero native value.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:110 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - initializes the clone with msg.sender as sponsor, sponsor-selected configuration, and factory-controlled treasury and raffle ID.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:176 Raffle.initialize - enforces one-time initialization and immutable factory authorization, screens destinations, stores configuration, and sets AwaitingPrize.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:123 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - populates raffleById, idByRaffle, and isRaffle before the external escrow call.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:128 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - calls the selected prize contract's safeTransferFrom(sponsor, raffle, prizeTokenId).\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:416 Raffle.onERC721Received - accepts only AwaitingPrize with the configured token caller, token ID, sponsor as from, and factory as operator; sets Active and returns the receiver selector.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:129 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - requires ownerOf(prizeTokenId) to report the clone and the clone's status to be Active.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:136 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - emits RaffleCreated and returns the clone address; all preceding state persists only if the call succeeds.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Commit the registered, initialized, active raffle and emit RaffleCreated before returning its address.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 128,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"prizeToken selects the external escrow target; prizeTokenId selects its asset; msg.sender supplies the transfer source and stored sponsor. sponsorRecipient, reserveEntries, and endTime become clone configuration. The implementation, quote token, treasury, and raffle ID are not supplied by the sponsor.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Crosses from factory-controlled deployment and registry state into an untrusted prize contract. Review depends on callback authentication, independent ownership/status checks, fixed implementation dispatch, and atomic rollback.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"A prize address without deployed code is rejected before cloning or querying ERC-721 support.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - accepts the typed sponsor configuration under nonReentrant.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:155 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - passes params.prizeToken to _requireContract.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:184 RaffleFactory._requireContract - reverts NotContract(account) when account.code.length is zero.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert NotContract(prizeToken), leaving no raffle or registry mutation.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 184,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The sponsor-selected prizeToken address is inspected directly for deployed code.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Establishes the minimum executable-target requirement before making interface and asset-transfer calls.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"A zero sponsor recipient is rejected before raffle deployment.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - dispatches to parameter validation.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:155 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - first requires deployed prize-token code.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:156 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - reverts ZeroAddress when sponsorRecipient is zero.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert ZeroAddress without creating a raffle.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 156,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"params.sponsorRecipient reaches the zero-address recipient check unchanged.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Protects the immutable recipient used for sponsor proceeds and returned prizes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Selecting known protocol infrastructure as the prize contract is rejected.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - enters parameter validation.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:155 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - requires prize-token code and a nonzero sponsor recipient.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:158 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - compares prizeToken with the factory, quote token, VRF wrapper, implementation, and registered raffles.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:161 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - reverts UnsafeProtocolDestination(prizeToken) on a match.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Reject the selected prize target with UnsafeProtocolDestination.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 158,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"params.prizeToken is compared against immutable protocol addresses and the isRaffle registry.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Separates arbitrary external prize contracts from same-factory protocol contracts before external dispatch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Selecting the prize contract or known protocol infrastructure as sponsor recipient is rejected.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - enters parameter validation.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:155 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - passes code, nonzero-recipient, and prize-target checks.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:164 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - compares sponsorRecipient with the factory, quote token, wrapper, selected prize token, implementation, and registered raffles.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:168 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - reverts UnsafeProtocolDestination(sponsorRecipient) on a match.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Reject the immutable sponsor recipient with UnsafeProtocolDestination.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 164,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The sponsor-selected recipient and prizeToken jointly determine the destination rejection condition.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Screens destinations that would later receive sponsor assets, including existing raffle clones.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"The selected prize contract is queried for ERC-721 support; a false response or failed call rejects creation, and malformed return data fails decoding.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - dispatches to _validateCreateParams.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:155 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - passes code and destination checks.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:172 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - makes a static supportsInterface(type(IERC721).interfaceId) call to the sponsor-selected contract and decodes a bool.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:174 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - converts an external-call failure into UnsupportedPrizeToken; malformed return-data decoding instead reverts in the caller.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:177 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - reverts UnsupportedPrizeToken if the decoded result is false.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert before cloning because ERC-721 support was not successfully reported.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 172,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"prizeToken selects the static-call target; its implementation controls the returned support assertion, revert behavior, and return-data encoding.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This is the first untrusted contract response consumed by creation. A successful interface assertion permits further execution but does not itself establish escrow behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"A zero reserve entry threshold is rejected after token-interface validation.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - calls _validateCreateParams.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:172 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - requires the prize contract to report ERC-721 support.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:178 RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams - reverts ZeroReserveEntries when reserveEntries is zero.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert ZeroReserveEntries before deploying the raffle.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 178,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The ABI-decoded uint128 params.reserveEntries reaches the nonzero threshold check.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Constrains sponsor-selected economic configuration before it becomes immutable clone state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"A sale end at or before the creation block timestamp is rejected.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - validates token, destinations, interface support, and reserve.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:99 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - reads block.timestamp.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:100 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - reverts InvalidEndTime when params.endTime is not strictly future.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert InvalidEndTime(currentTime, endTime) before incrementing raffleCount.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 100,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The sponsor's uint64 endTime is compared directly with the current block timestamp.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Establishes the sale-time boundary and ensures a fresh clone cannot request a draw during its creation transaction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"A future sale end more than 30 days away is rejected.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - passes configuration validation.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:100 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - requires endTime to be strictly future.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:101 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - computes uint256(endTime) minus block.timestamp.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:102 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - compares the duration with MAX_SALE_DURATION, defined as 30 days, and reverts SaleDurationTooLong if exceeded.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert SaleDurationTooLong before deploying or registering a raffle.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 102,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"params.endTime determines the computed prospective sale duration.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Bounds the sponsor-controlled sale interval and associated escrow duration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Configuration that passes factory validation can still fail the clone's additional destination checks during initialization, rolling back deployment and the ID increment.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - passes factory-level configuration and timing checks.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:105 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - increments the ID and deploys the fixed-target clone.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:110 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - supplies the original caller as sponsor and forwards the selected prize and recipient.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:177 Raffle.initialize - passes the fresh-clone and factory-caller checks and sets initialized.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:187 Raffle.initialize - screens sponsor, protocolTreasury, and sponsorRecipient in that order through _isProtocolDestination.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:593 Raffle._isProtocolDestination - includes the fresh clone itself, factory, quote token, wrapper, prospective prize token, implementation, and registered raffles.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:188 Raffle.initialize - the first failing destination check reverts UnsafeProtocolDestination; corresponding treasury and recipient reverts occur at lines 191 and 194.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert clone initialization and undo the clone creation and raffleCount increment.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 187,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"msg.sender becomes the checked sponsor; prizeToken participates in every destination comparison; sponsorRecipient is also checked against the newly deployed clone. Reachable examples include a prize contract sponsoring itself or a recipient chosen as the predicted new clone address. Selecting a contract treasury as prize also reaches the treasury check if earlier checks pass.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"The clone enforces additional address relationships unavailable or unchecked during factory validation. These checks determine sponsor authority and immutable asset destinations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"The prize contract can reject the escrow transfer, causing all creation effects to roll back.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - passes validation and deploys the clone.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:176 Raffle.initialize - stores configuration and sets AwaitingPrize.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:123 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - writes the three registry mappings.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:128 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - calls prizeToken.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, raffle, prizeTokenId); any propagated external revert aborts creation.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Propagate the escrow-call failure and revert deployment, initialization, registration, and any nested changes.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 128,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The sponsor controls the called prize contract and token ID; the source is fixed to the original msg.sender and the destination to the new clone. A standards-compliant prize contract also enforces its ownership and transfer-approval requirements here.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This non-static call executes untrusted code after registry writes. The factory does not catch transfer failures, so correctness relies on transaction atomicity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"An incorrect or duplicate NFT receiver callback is rejected without activating the clone.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:128 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - enters the supplied prize contract's transfer implementation.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:416 Raffle.onERC721Received - receives the token's callback directly or an attempted callback through another contract.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:421 Raffle.onERC721Received - checks AwaitingPrize, actual caller identity, configured token ID, sponsor as from, and factory as operator.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:425 Raffle.onERC721Received - reverts UnexpectedPrize if any condition fails, including a repeated callback after activation.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert the invalid receiver callback; creation also reverts if the prize contract propagates that failure.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 421,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The selected token controls callback arguments and sequencing. Its actual caller identity is checked separately from operator, from, and tokenId; callback data bytes are unused.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This boundary authorizes the AwaitingPrize-to-Active transition. A token that catches a rejected callback must still satisfy the factory's final ownership and activation checks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"A returned escrow call is followed by an ownership query; unreadable ownership or an owner other than the clone aborts creation.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:128 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - the selected prize contract's safeTransferFrom returns.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:129 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - statically calls ownerOf(params.prizeTokenId) and decodes the returned address; external-call or decoding failure propagates.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:130 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - reverts PrizeEscrowVerificationFailed if the reported owner is not the clone.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert creation on an unsuccessful ownership query or a failed ownership comparison.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 129,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The sponsor-selected prizeToken and prizeTokenId determine the ownership query. The selected contract supplies the owner response compared against the factory-created clone address.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"A successful transfer call or receiver callback alone does not complete creation. This independent postcondition consumes another response from the same untrusted prize contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Even when the prize contract reports the clone as owner, creation fails unless the clone remains Active.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:128 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - escrow transfer returns.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:129 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - the prize contract reports the clone as owner.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:132 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - reads status from the fixed-implementation clone.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:133 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - reverts PrizeEscrowVerificationFailed when status is not Active, including an omitted activation callback or a transient cancellation.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert the entire creation because its activation postcondition failed.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 132,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The selected prize contract's callback behavior determines whether the clone was activated and whether nested actions changed its status before this check.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"The final status gate validates clone state independently of the prize contract's ownership assertion and makes callback-induced cancellation incompatible with successful creation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Reentry into factory creation from the prize contract is blocked before a second raffle can be deployed.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - the outer call holds the factory's nonReentrant guard.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:128 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - the selected prize contract executes and attempts another createRaffle call.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:97 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - the nested call enters the same guard before parameter validation.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:88 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBeforeView - detects the entered factory storage slot and reverts ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Reject nested factory creation; the outer creation survives only if the external caller handles the nested failure and completes escrow.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 97,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The sponsor-selected prize implementation can choose nested creation arguments, but the guard rejects the call before they reach validation or deployment.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"Protects factory ID allocation and registration across the untrusted external-call boundary. The guard belongs to the factory, independently of each clone's guard.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"After activating the clone during escrow, the selected prize contract or a helper can buy entries before createRaffle returns.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:128 RaffleFactory.createRaffle - the selected token executes during escrow.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:416 Raffle.onERC721Received - a valid callback sets the clone to Active at line 428.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:209 Raffle.buyEntries - the token or a helper enters the clone's independent nonReentrant guard.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:215 Raffle.buyEntries - checks Active status, sale time, nonzero recipient and count, and the entry-count bound.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:223 Raffle.buyEntries - computes entryCount times 1,000,000 raw quote-token units.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:224 Raffle.buyEntries - pulls canonical USDC from the nested caller into the clone.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:227 SafeERC20._safeTransferFrom - performs the token call; failed calls or unsuccessful return values revert